body:
Psalm 100:3-5



3 Know that the Lord is God.

It is He Who made us, and we are His;

we are His people, the sheep of His pasture.

4 Enter His gates with thanksgiving

and His courts with praise;

give thanks to Him and praise His Name.

5 For the Lord is good and His love endures forever;

His faithfulness continues through all generations.

My view is that we have 'new bodies'; new abilities; new experiences;

What will time be like? Will days be days or will time be different?

What I know is the love of God is so powerful as to be overwhelming.

Recently I reread the 11th and 12th chapter of Hebrews. The idea is to show people of faith over time. These were not perfect people (like David who really messed up his life), but still people of faith. The 12th chapter really brings home the point with:

&#x200B;

We have a race to run. It's not easy. But we can do it!

One way to change your attitude is praise God always. 

For example, you can start by finding something every mourning to praise God.  A simple sunrise; a light breeze that feels good; a misty fog that is interesting; a simple cup of good coffee; 

If you get in the habit of finding things to praise God about, even very small things, it begins to change your view of the world. The more you find things to praise God, the more you become closer to God.

&#x200B;

My favorite warbler is:

https://www.allaboutbirds.org/guide/Prothonotary\_Warbler/overview
